WEBVTT

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.480
It's been a while, kid.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.900
I've come to retrieve Hana.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:21.370
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:28.540
I'm watching an endless dream

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.010
Aren't you watching too?

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:42.350
It's always close by no matter how far away it seems

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:49.190
Can't you see it too?

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.610
The things you can't normally say

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:57.370
The things you try to express

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.870
The things you're willing to fight for

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:05.580
Standing on your own two feet

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:12.260
The night sky illuminates them all

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:19.390
The first flash of lightning

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:25.730
This is our battle to fight

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:33.070
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:41.530
This dream will absolutely come true

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.580
Manatsu Daichi,

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:50.840
do you have any idea what you're trying to do?

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:56.840
Sleeping within this ship are thousands of young men...

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.390
Young men who have been entrusted with humanity's future.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:05.770
You're trying to destroy not just their lives, but the very future of humanity.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.680
No!

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:12.070
The captain is trying to save their lives.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.070
What is this "life" you speak of?

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.400
The boys sleeping within this ship

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:24.660
will wake up alone in the universe and locked forever inside this iron prison.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.830
They'll sleep for thousands, no,

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:33.710
tens of thousands of years, perhaps forever, inside this spaceship.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.340
That isn't life.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:43.010
The way I felt in that cold spaceship, just watching time pass...

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.470
I don't want anyone else to experience that.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.270
It's miserable.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:54.980
I'm sure they all want to run around, full of life, on that blue planet below!

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.190
And I'm sure the captain will make that happen.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.910
I cannot imagine that kid is prepared for that.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.910
Put down your gun.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.120
Pull that trigger, and you'll blow up the whole <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.500
This is a detonator.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.670
If I die, it activates.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:24.760
Bear in mind that every soul aboard the <i>Tenkaido</i> is currently my hostage.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:30.140
I can't imagine that a member of the Ark Faction would destroy

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.600
all of the young men sleeping here.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:37.150
With humanity's future at stake, do you really think we wouldn't prepare a spare?

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:43.070
We're ready to make some sacrifices if it means saving humanity from extinction.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.700
Don't underestimate us, kid!

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.080
I've run a trace simulation on the enemy's actions

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.750
to predict where the bombs are.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.300
But given that he's been moving about freely,

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.470
we should assume he has inside help.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.140
And we have to assume there are other bombs.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.970
Forward the projected locations to the bomb disposal team.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.270
Roger.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.230
Don't move.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.150
"Midsummer's Knights"?

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.860
You cannot save this planet without an iron resolve,

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.110
Manatsu Daichi.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.150
Especially not you.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:24.950
Hana!

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:40.670
We've no intention of needlessly harming anybody aboard the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:45.340
Our primary objective is securing Mutou Hana.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.140
And if Pointer screws up?

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:53.350
At the very least, he should help us with our little <i>problem</i>.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:58.060
Operation Summer will not proceed. That shall be seen to.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:04.650
Yes, the <i>Blume</i> is ours.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.660
The Meaning
of a Captain

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:27.300
Sorry, but today's concert isn't an abreaction.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.220
The <i>Blume</i> is in orbit.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:37.100
It'll pose a bit of a problem should they decide to attack us.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:41.360
It's theoretically possible to destroy an ego block

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.940
if they convert their Orgone energy into pure physical energy.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.280
There's a good chance

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.120
they'll use the <i>Blume</i>'s Entangle Link to destroy the Cocoon inside <i>Oberon</i>.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.620
That would be devastating!

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.160
Exactly...

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.710
We need to make every effort to prevent that.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.210
Ai, go up there and defeat them.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.170
Why Ai?

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.460
She's the only one whose face they don't know.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.380
I can't believe it...

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:09.590
Using an idol who hides her face with sunglasses for an act of terorism?

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:12.760
Zin's singularity will be helpful.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.600
Have him share it with you by telepathic kiss.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.730
I can't believe it!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:23.190
If the press sees that, there'll be total chaos.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.360
Hey, Ai?

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:30.820
I think I like the way you try so hard in this video.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.780
Well, you know...

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.580
It's my job.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.210
Kiss scenes are also part of my job, huh?

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.190
I found a good one.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.240
What's wrong, Pitz?

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.580
This is Manatsu.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.200
What's wrong, Captain?

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:18.950
Hana's been kidnapped.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.420
It was Hirose, from Salty Dog.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:27.630
He has a detonator for the bombs placed on <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:31.550
Governor Yomatsuri, I'll send you the route we expect him to take.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.430
Roger.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.720
I'll forward it to security.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.930
Security, listen well!

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.100
From the projected escape path,

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.020
he's likely escaped into the engine block.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:46.320
The detonator is linked to his vitals,

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.650
so use of firearms is prohibited!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.440
He has kidnapped Mutou Hana.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.280
What now?

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.950
A meteoroid is on a collision course for the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.870
Spectral analysis has identified its composition.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:05.130
Inconel... Probably the remnants of a spaceship.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.880
I don't see this debris in our catalog.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.380
It isn't in our catalog?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.880
Bearing: 736.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.590
Relative distance: 300,000 meters.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:14.760
Relative speed: 400 meters per second.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.550
We can't dodge it.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.220
Collision in 750 seconds.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:21.350
Estimated mass: 1,200 kilograms.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.770
Impact energy: 96 megajoules.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:27.440
That's enough energy to penetrate the debris bumper!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:29.610
Akari?

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:33.900
A large piece of debris is heading for us.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:35.240
Debris?

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:38.200
Just get Hana back as soon as possible.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.160
Otherwise, I won't know what Pitz is saying!

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:42.910
What's going on with Pitz?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:47.920
Just before we found the debris, Pitz started freaking out.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.420
Because Hana was kidnapped?

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:54.300
No, this is just my intuition as a magical girl,

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.970
but something else is going on here.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.720
I'll handle the debris.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:00.180
You follow Hirose.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:01.100
Roger.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:03.680
I'm counting on you, Daichi.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:04.390
Roger.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.980
Governor, Teppei is headed for the Nebula Engine.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.820
Have him launch as soon as he's ready!

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:11.730
Roger.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.120
Target sighted.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.580
Commencing destruction.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.420
Target has vanished.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.380
No, there's more.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.050
A new meteoroid, incoming.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.350
Bearing: 927.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.480
Relative distance: 350,000 meters.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.810
Relative speed: 420 meters per second.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.400
Impact in 833 seconds.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:53.070
There's no record of this debris in the catalog, either.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.110
Estimated mass: 2,800 kilograms.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:59.280
There's no way we couldn't detect the orbit of debris this size...

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:00.910
Footage incoming.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:03.450
Commencing destruction.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.880
Target has vanished.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:15.630
A second one?

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.510
Oh my, did my test attract some attention?

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.470
But... But...

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.480
There's plenty of debris in orbit!

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:34.190
I have all kinds of toys ready to gift to my fans!

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:35.570
Violent...

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:36.900
Attacking...

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:39.410
Tickets to hell!

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.410
More debris incoming.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.330
Thirty-five in total.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.410
Thirty-six.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:46.370
There's still more!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:47.790
What?

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.420
What's going on?

00:10:58.130 --> 00:10:59.760
Relative distance: 320,000 meters.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.590
Relative speed: 420 meters per second.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.680
Impact in 780 seconds.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.270
Destroying.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.060
Not bad...

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:16.030
But how about this?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.030
They dodged?

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:26.580
No!

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.330
This is the Nebula.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.460
Some of the debris is heading your way!

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.290
<i>Tenkaido</i>, do you read me?

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:38.920
Propulsion, communication, and ejection systems are all down...

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:40.970
The Nebula Engine has been hit.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.970
The debris has passed the Nebula, and is heading for the <i>Tenkaido</i>!

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.350
More debris!

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.560
Are you okay, Teppei?

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:50.560
Teppei?

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.560
The communication system is offline?

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.270
Captain, come in!

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.400
This is Manatsu.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.990
The Nebula has been knocked out of commission!

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:01.490
Teppei?

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:03.820
The debris is on course for the <i>Tenkaido</i>!

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:05.570
Head out in the Earth.

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:06.870
But, Hana...

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:10.450
At this rate, the <i>Tenkaido</i> itself is in danger.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.420
Understood.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.960
Even more debris has appeared.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.960
What is Pitz saying?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.800
Forty-seven... Forty-eight... Forty-nine...

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:20.920
It keeps coming!

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:21.630
It can't be!

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:25.760
Bingo!

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.180
MM bus signal detected.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.600
Epicenter identified.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:31.770
It's...

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.730
Inside the transport ship <i>Nipper</i>?

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:39.110
Security Team 64, get to space port <i>Nipper</i>.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.490
There's no end to them.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:50.290
Governor, there's even more debris coming!

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.660
Of all the times for this to happen...

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.420
What's going on?

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:09.010
The main event is only beginning.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.850
Over five hundred pieces of debris incoming.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.480
They're coming in at relative speed: 620.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.440
We can't stop them all...

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.330
Captain, we'll use the Boosted Plazmagnum.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:34.080
But we haven't even tested it!

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.290
There's no other way to survive this.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:39.250
You can do it, right?

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:42.920
Understood.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.140
Boosted Plazmagnum, stand by!

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.920
Boosted Plazmagnum, scramble!

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:43.110
The Marine Gate...

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.790
Target confirmed.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.880
Boosted Plazmagnum, ready to go.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.000
Wait, Captain...

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.590
We need to get the Nebula out of there, or Teppei will...

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.680
The Nebula can't move.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:18.560
Its propulsion system has been destroyed, and we can't contact it.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.690
The ejection system is probably damaged, too.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:26.690
But...

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:29.900
If we don't fire now, it's over.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:30.990
It's impossible!

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.820
He can't do it!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.540
You go to the <i>Blume</i>,

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:41.290
and promise me you'll save humanity's chosen.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:43.170
Hey!

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:45.630
Wake up!

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:52.260
Only those with the necessary resolve can save humanity!

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.690
You understand, don't you, Captain?

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.240
Don't hesitate!

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.360
Fire!

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:49.570
He fired.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:59.080
An amazing amount of energy...

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:02.200
Is this that boy's power?

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.790
It may be just as King said.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.130
Indeed.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:13.340
We can entrust our hopes to that team.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:25.520
All objects in the firing radius have been annihilated...

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.110
Teppei...

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.480
What is this?

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.860
There's a signal where the Nebula was destroyed.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:39.700
Is this...

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.300
The Nebula Engine?

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:00.140
Teppei...

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.520
I'm alive?

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:13.070
DC?

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.000
What is that machine?

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:33.550
What is that light coming from the Orgone energy?

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:37.920
This is Matsui, with Security Team 64.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:41.800
We've found a suspicious object in the <i>Nipper's</i> cargo room.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:43.850
A Machine Goodfellow?

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.430
And it's active!

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.520
Destroy that capsule!

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:49.140
Hurry!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:50.810
R-Roger!

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:54.690
I hate it when my fans ambush me.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.370
The event's over.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:12.750
This is Security Team 64.

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.750
We destroyed the capsule, but the object fled.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.170
We will continue searching for the bombs.

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.910
Had our positions been reversed...

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.460
I would have fired 2.5 seconds earlier.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.630
You still aren't strong enough, Captain.

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.140
Let's get Hana back.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:04.510
Yeah.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:59.360
My mission is to kidnap Mutou Hana and to eliminate you.

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:02.320
Answer me one thing.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:09.280
Did you know Arashi Teppei would survive that?

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:15.540
Or are you the kind of man who would let one of his friends die?

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:17.630
Answer me!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:25.800
I thought I was going to kill Teppei with my own hands.

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:29.390
I wasn't going to "let him die."

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:32.600
If he'd died,

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:36.440
it would have been because I killed him.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:42.030
But I couldn't afford to hesitate there.

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:50.450
I don't like you.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.740
I hate you!

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:55.620
But...

00:21:57.250 --> 00:22:01.800
Can you really defeat our enemy?

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:08.430
Can you really save Earth?

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:15.640
If you really can...

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:21.480
Please.

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:24.360
My father and my brother...

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:27.280
Save the planet where everyone lives.

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:30.990
If you really can...

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:37.910
Please save them, Captain Earth!

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:17.100
At last, the time has come to destroy the enemy dreadnaught <i>Oberon</i>.

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:20.810
That very moment, Alonzo tells us that the Planetary Gears are

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.310
launching an all-out attack.

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:23.980
We're running out of time.

00:24:23.980 --> 00:24:28.690
But Salty Dog's ultimate weapon stands before us.

00:24:28.690 --> 00:24:30.190
Why are you getting in our way?

00:24:30.190 --> 00:24:32.450
This plan is for the Earth's protection!

